    "project_type": "ml_competition",
    "description": "\ud83d\ude80 Project Description: Wunder Challenge LOB Predictorium (OFI-Alpha & Strict Packaging)\n\n1. Project Objective \ud83c\udfaf\nDevelop a high-precision forecasting system to predict dual future price-movement targets (t0, t1) using Limit Order Book (LOB) sequences. The success metric is a Weighted Pearson Correlation >= 0.34.\n\n2. Data & Alpha Engineering \ud83d\udcc8\nInput: Parquet sequences of 1000 timesteps with 32 features. \nCRITICAL ALPHA: Raw LOB data is non-stationary. The data loader MUST convert raw bid/ask volumes into Order Flow Imbalance (OFI) features and normalize all price levels relative to the mid-price. Output shape must remain strictly (batch, 1000, 32). Respect warm-up logic (steps 0-98) and predict only for steps 99-999.\n\n3. Architecture: Temporal Fusion DeepLOB \ud83e\udde0\nSpatial Feature Extraction: CNN layers (DeepLOB style) to extract spatial relationships.\nTemporal/Sequence: Utilize LSTM networks or Temporal Self-Attention, as sequence modeling is mathematically proven to outperform standard MLPs on LOB data.\n\n4. Loss Function: Direct Correlation \ud83c\udfaf\nDo NOT use MSE. Implement a custom Weighted Pearson Loss function that directly maximizes correlation. Apply amplitude weighting (w_i = |y_i|) as per competition rules. Enforce output clipping to the [-6, 6] range.\n\n5. Strict Deployment & Packaging Constraints \ud83d\udce6\nDocker Pathing Fix: The inference script (solution.py) MUST load the ONNX model using a strict relative path: `onnx_path = 'model.onnx'` (no os.path.dirname logic).\nPrerun Test: The pipeline must include a local `prerun.py` script that instantiates PredictionModel and tests a dummy (1, 1000, 32) array.\nFinal Deliverable: The packaging script MUST create a flat `submission.zip` containing EXACTLY three files: solution.py, model.onnx, and utils.py. Actual solution.py and utils.py in root. solution.py should have wundern simplest path to model.onnx. No subdirectories or extra files are allowed.",
